{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1426553-predator-type-when-a-new-vampire-gets-one","id":1426553,"title":"Predator type, when a new vampire gets one?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-11-29T03:20:56-08:00","id":1426553,"title":"Predator type, when a new vampire gets one?","content":"Do fledglings get a Predator Type? How vampire old do you have to be to have one?<br /> <br /> Some Predator Types imply very recent fledglings, like the Cleaver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26402-luizborges","name":"luizborges","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-29T03:34:38-08:00","id":1426556,"title":"","content":"You get a predator type at character creation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's good for giving you a few ideas, but it's primarily a device for game convenience, it doesn't reflect the reality of how vampires actually feed. It'd be too restrictive for that. Treat it as such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 11-29-2020, 06:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-29T04:11:30-08:00","id":1426560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1426553-predator-type-when-a-new-vampire-gets-one?p=1426556#post1426556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You get a predator type at character creation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That was my understanding also, but after some back and forth on discord, some people pointed me to the last paragraph on p.149 that says: &quot;fresh bloodsuckers, like thin bloods and many fledglings don't get a predator type&quot;, and I got confused. I think that for a fledgling to no get one it must be a specific call from the ST (like narrating the embrace, and so on).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26402-luizborges","name":"luizborges","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-29T04:28:57-08:00","id":1426563,"title":"","content":"Set a time period to give them a predator type then. Like two weeks or a month or... the first drink. Players generally step into their game after their character has gone through the introductory phase with their sire (which may take between a night and fifty years...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-29T07:09:29-08:00","id":1426580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1426553-predator-type-when-a-new-vampire-gets-one?p=1426563#post1426563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Set a time period to give them a predator type then. Like two weeks or a month or... the first drink. Players generally step into their game after their character has gone through the introductory phase with their sire (which may take between a night and fifty years...)</div> </div> </div> </div>This. A vampire who has gone through any training their sire may provide will have developed a predator type. Unless your character is dependant on their sire and hasn't been released into society you have a predator type.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-29T14:32:21-08:00","id":1426624,"title":"","content":"My players who were all new to Vampire (apart from one) wanted to really play the embrace and the turn from human to vampire and to slowly find out what is happening to their characters. So I did the following:<br /> <br /> * As the players are embraced they get 1 clan discipline at level 1.<br /> * A few nights later, based on their Wits level (Level 4, 1 night later, level 3, 1\u00bd night later etc...the quicker to adapt the faster you get it - This the players did not know when they created their characters) you get another clan discipline at level 1.<br /> * After the first week, you get one of these disciplines to level 2.<br /> <br /> During this time, their sires were helping them to hunt and find out which predator style they preferred. I had briefly explained the various styles, but no player wanted to know what they got out of it. So each player chose their style based on that.<br /> <br /> So after approximate 1 week after embrace, based on the main skills used to hunt, they started to gain the benefits one after another over time and approximately a month after embrace they had the whole package.<br /> <br /> My players loved this waya d this is now standard in the three groups i play/game master.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-29T17:05:48-08:00","id":1426638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1426553-predator-type-when-a-new-vampire-gets-one?p=1426556#post1426556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You get a predator type at character creation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's good for giving you a few ideas, but it's primarily a device for game convenience, it doesn't reflect the reality of how vampires actually feed. It'd be too restrictive for that. Treat it as such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, some predator types lock characters into that feeding style (animal only and consensual only, I forget if others)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-29T18:11:41-08:00","id":1426645,"title":"","content":"I would not pinpoint exactly when a vampire develops a predatory type.<br /> Like others said - it\u00b4s what the vampire does what it feels is the most satisfying/comforting/&quot;moral&quot; mode to aquire Vitae.<br /> I\u00b4d reckon to let the predatory type tell a story about the character. But I dislike that some lock the character into a place as there are more motivations to be a &quot;vegetarian&quot; or consensualist.<br /> - We have one consensualist, who does not because of beeing &quot;humane&quot; but out of the thrill of endangering the masquerade.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-29T20:08:03-08:00","id":1426655,"title":"","content":"I also think that requiring some predator styles to have restricted prey to match their style removes any drama from the choice to feed that way. it's fine if the player voluntarily chooses restricted prey, but requiring it doesn't work for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T05:48:27-08:00","id":1426691,"title":"","content":"My current game played through the embrace, and I had them pick up their Predator type after the second session as kindred. It let them have an opportunity to respond to the change and figure out what they wanted to do in order to get blood. Their mentors also pressed them to figure out the best way to feed given their individual skill sets and psychological predilections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24680-jrrparker","name":"JRRParker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T14:05:47-08:00","id":1426736,"title":"","content":"Hum... I don't usually keeps the sire around for long. Usually we just narrate the before embrace, the embrace, and some instructions to live on and then they go in their separate ways, all in the prelude to the story. The sire is sometimes within reach and give some hints or pointers, but unless they have him/her as mawla or something (which a player in my group has) they don't stick for long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26402-luizborges","name":"luizborges","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T14:38:47-08:00","id":1426859,"title":"","content":"This is an interesting point, from the background given in the various books the impression I get is that a vampire would learn the how to hunt from their side and from this would go with a variation on this they feel comfortable with.<br /> <br /> However if they had to learn how to feed by themselves they would be more likely to choose an extreme to start with before settling into a more nuanced hunting method.<br /> <br /> I'm in the final stages of setting up prepping a vampire roleplay where the characters start as ghouls before becoming vampires and learning such ins and outs of the Vampire life. Any ideas for how I should run this with the group when they are embraced would be welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11469-capussa","name":"Capussa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}